   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">&gt; sessionInfo()<br>R version 3.1.1 (2014-07-10)\r\nPlatform: x86_64-w64-mingw32/x64 (64-bit)\r\n\r\nlocale:\r\n[1] LC_COLLATE=English_United States.1252  LC_CTYPE=English_United States.1252   \r\n[3] LC_MONETARY=English_United States.1252 LC_NUMERIC=C                          \r\n[5] LC_TIME=English_United States.1252    \r\n\r\nattached base packages:\r\n[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     \r\n\r\nother attached packages:\r\n[1] shinyapps_0.3.63 dplyr_0.3.0.2    data.table_1.9.4 shiny_0.10.2.2  \r\n\r\nloaded via a namespace (and not attached):\r\n [1] assertthat_0.1  chron_2.3-45    DBI_0.3.1       digest_0.6.4    htmltools_0.2.6\r\n [6] httpuv_1.3.0    lazyeval_0.1.9  magrittr_1.0.1  mime_0.2        parallel_3.1.1 \r\n[11] plyr_1.8.1      R6_2.0          Rcpp_0.11.3     RCurl_1.95-4.3  reshape2_1.4   \r\n[16] RJSONIO_1.3-0   stringr_0.6.2   tools_3.1.1     xtable_1.7-3   </pre></span><br><br>Thanks <span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Yihui Xie </span></span>and everyone, I have resolved the problem. <br><br>Instead of using fread the Google sheet directly from the URL, which only work with Windows:<br><br><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">fileURL </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1HqkFzMxhXwE2usiyhF-Qorje-uNWUdB7l3oz4TFzuSo/export?format=csv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1HqkFzMxhXwE2usiyhF-Qorje-uNWUdB7l3oz4TFzuSo/export?format%3Dcsv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792364144035000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1A5-HVXE8UEFQKYqAkQuRj\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1HqkFzMxhXwE2usiyhF-Qorje-uNWUdB7l3oz4TFzuSo/export?format=csv</a>&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>DF </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fread</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fileURL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> header</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">downloader:download the Google sheet as CSV into local drive then fread it (work with Windows and Ubuntu):</span><br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">downloader</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fileURL </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1HqkFzMxhXwE2usiyhF-Qorje-uNWUdB7l3oz4TFzuSo/export?format=csv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1HqkFzMxhXwE2usiyhF-Qorje-uNWUdB7l3oz4TFzuSo/export?format%3Dcsv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792364144035000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1A5-HVXE8UEFQKYqAkQuRj\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1HqkFzMxhXwE2usiyhF-Qorje-uNWUdB7l3oz4TFzuSo/export?format=csv</a>&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#DF &lt;- fread(fileURL, header=TRUE)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>localCSV </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;./gs.csv&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>download</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fileURL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> localCSV</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mode </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;wb&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>DF </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fread</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">localCSV</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> header</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">View</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">DF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>The next question will be how to tell the server not to overwrite the download Google sheet if no change has made.<br></div></span></code><br><br></div>"
